Fall back to the carrier's DEFAULT APN when it marks no IA entry

The CP will not ask the network for an attach APN itself, so an empty one
leaves it attached on the HSS's subscribed default with no context of its own.
The IMS PDN that follows is then refused -- MATCH_ALL_RULE_NOT_ALLOWED (2253)
where the network's policy forbids the catch-all URSP rule, cause 133 where the
ESM piggyback failed -- and there is no VoLTE until the user sets
gsm.initial-eps-bearer-apn on a NetworkManager profile by hand.

Only 77 of the 588 carriers in the database mark an IA entry at all. Telus is
one of them, which is why it alone worked; Fizz and AT&T mark none, fell through
to the empty APN and needed the override. Android falls back to the DEFAULT
entry for those carriers, confirmed against this CP on the wire: both stacks
were captured mid-attach sending the entry they carry data on -- Telus its IA
'sp.telus.com' (types 0x117, pdp 3), Fizz its DEFAULT 'mobile.bm' (types 0x7,
pdp 1).

